each whose body is a struct of mappings, in the forward direction, that
neither maps nor drops a field the element has and the target's element
lacks: still an error. Only a copy body drops the rest of the element by
derivation, since it has nowhere to write a drop; a struct body does.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...close({id!: string, is_enabled!: bool})]
})
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: close({
	u!: [...close({key!: string})]
})

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		u: _each(v0_0.u, {key: _item.id})
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: close({u!: [...close({key!: string})]})
-- out/error --
error[E0347]: 0.0 declares is_enabled and 1.0 does not, and nothing maps it: write <field>: _item.is_enabled to move it, or is_enabled: _drop
 --> history/1.0.thema:8:3
  |
8 |         u: _each(v0_0.u, {key: _item.id})
  |         ^
